{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1yDZfCr4g79oswir3oE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with one confirmed bug and one area I could not test.\n\n**Confirmed bug (filed and logged):** after I changed the 13 Nov expense's tag from Food to Transport in the editor, the history row showed \"Purchase Reason: Transport\", but Analytics → Categories (Total range) still put all $65 under Food. No Transport category appeared.\n\n**Verified working:**\n- Editing the amount from $40 to $45 saved, persisted after leaving the screen, and updated the total to $65.\n- Analytics total, the Today pill ($1.67 = 35 / 21 days), and the savings card (Spent $65, Available 35%) all agree.\n- Cancelling an edit with \"Tap to exit\" discarded the typed $99 and kept the saved $45.\n- The budget dates (11 Nov – 4 Dec, 20 days remaining) match the preconditions.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- **Period start day:** I could not find a start-day setting in Settings, Extra features, or the Edit Budget / new-period flow, so that build change is untested.\n- **Past periods:** the list was empty, so no past-period editing was tested.\n- **Landscape clipping:** I filed a report for clipping on the home screen in landscape. The developer could not reproduce it with my steps.\n\nI did not create a new budget period. I opened the new-period draft and closed it without pressing Next. The sign-off confidence is 0.5 because the start-day item was untested."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1026, "cache_read_input_tokens": 270305, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1026}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool